<DescriptionTexts>Change your Xbox 360 console settings, including display, audio, language, and remote control.\0Protect younger family members by limiting content, communications, and online interactions.

You can adjust settings for the console or for individual profiles.\0Move or delete saved games, profiles, and other items on Xbox 360 storage devices.\0Connect to Xbox LIVE or your home network. Set up wireless connections and test network settings.\0Manage your connection to a Windows Media Center PC.

To connect to a PC running media sharing software, open your video, music, or picture library. \0Change the settings for your Xbox LIVE Vision camera.\0Start the original system setup.

You can't run initial setup if Family Settings are enabled.\0</DescriptionTexts>
